messages:
maria: quick a11y pass on the new dashboard build. 3 small things I ran into: 1) skip link is present but invisible when focused, 2) chart legend colors fail 4.5:1 on light theme for small markers, 3) pagination controls in model table aren't announced properly by NVDA. sharing notes + a short screencap: https://assets.redwood/qa/skiplink-focus.mp4 :camera:

ben: thanks — good call. skip links should be visually hidden but revealed on focus. iirc we use the sr-only util that hides on focus; maybe it got overwritten. can you paste the selector?

maria: current markup: `<a href="#main" class="skip">Skip to main</a>` and the CSS relies on `.sr-only` but the class wasn't added. simple fix but worth adding a visual test.

nina: for legend contrast, do you have the hex values? chart lib uses these small swatches: #9ca3ff, #fbbf24, #6ee7b7. I suspect the purple on white is borderline for thin strokes.

maria: purple swatch #9ca3ff on white is ~3.8:1 as large area, but the stroke thickness makes it effectively lower. design prefers >=4.5:1 for small UI indicators. suggestion: darken to #6b7bff for the small markers only.

sean: pagination announce bug — reproducer: open models table, tab to pagination, use arrow keys to change page (we support arrow navigation), NVDA reads "button" but not the page number / position. looks like we don't update `aria-live` or `aria-current`. Could add `aria-live="polite"` on a hidden status element that updates "Page 2 of 12" when page changes.

a11y-bot: automated run: lighthouse-a11y summary: 5 failures found — labels (2), color-contrast (1), focus-visible (1), aria-roles (1). Full: https://ci.redwood/lh/1746009876

ben: CSS for skip-link reveal (proposal):

```
.skip {
  position: absolute;
  left: -9999px;
  top: auto;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.skip:focus, .skip:active {
  left: 12px;
  top: 12px;
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  padding: 8px 12px;
  background: var(--bg-elev);
  border-radius: 4px;
}
```

keeps it offscreen but visible on keyboard focus.

nina: for charts, instead of changing palette globally, can we add an outline for small markers? that helps sighted users without changing branding. but still need legend text contrast. maybe make legend text 14px medium and ensure >=4.5:1.

maria: outline for markers is good fallback. I'll check with design for token change. also please add `aria-label` to each legend item like `aria-label="Model A: 24%"` so screen reader users get context.

sean: pagination aria update snippet:

```
const live = document.getElementById('page-status');
function updatePage(page, total) {
  live.textContent = `Page ${page} of ${total}`;
}
```

`<div id="page-status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></div>`

should work and not steal focus.

ben: small label / role nit: filter chips are buttons but some have `role=listitem` leftover from old markup. that confuses AT. ensure chips are `<button>` with `aria-pressed` when toggleable.

a11y-bot: note: tests flagged `aria-pressed` missing on 3 filter chips.

nina: microcopy tweak: change "Clear" to "Clear all filters" for the toolbar button so screen reader users know scope.

maria: thanks. action plan:
1) ben: add skip CSS + ensure `.skip` is used (PR today)
2) nina: propose legend adjustments + fallback outline (design approval)
3) sean: add page-status live region + fix aria-current on active page (PR)
4) maria: small audit pass after PRs, run NVDA + VoiceOver quick checks

I'll file a ticket and link PRs: https://app.redwood/issue/INF-4921. tagging @frontend for visibility. :rocket:

sean: i'll also add an e2e that asserts `#page-status` text updates after clicking next so we don't regress.

ben: will include a visual regression screenshot for skip link focus state in the PR.

maria: perfect, thanks all. tiny wins but important :pray:
